:name: RAK4631, as the hardware actually is
:description: MBR, UICR, bootloader, SoftDevice and application, on erased flash.
:
: This is the machine that got the published binaries past the MBR. Every piece
: here was written at some point and none of them had ever been assembled into
: one machine, which is why each experiment hit a different missing thing and
: each looked like a separate dead end.
:
: Prepare the pieces first:
:
:   tools/renode/uf2tobin.py RAK_4631_repeater-v1.17.0-*.uf2 /tmp/rak.bin
:   tools/renode/softdevice.py s140_nrf52_6.1.1_softdevice.hex /tmp/s140.bin
:   curl -sLo /tmp/rak_boot.uf2 \
:     https://flasher.meshcore.io/firmware/wiscore_rak4631_board_bootloader-0.9.2-OTAFIX2.1.uf2
:   tools/renode/uf2split.py /tmp/rak_boot.uf2 /tmp/boot
:   tools/renode/ficr.py > /tmp/ficr_writes.txt
:   python3 -c "open('/tmp/erased_flash.bin','wb').write(b'\xff'*(1024*1024))"
:   python3 -c "open('/tmp/erased_uicr.bin','wb').write(b'\xff'*4096)"
:
: The OTAFIX bootloader package is where UICR comes from, and UICR is what tells
: the MBR where the bootloader is. Without it the MBR reads zeros and hands over
: to address 0.

i @tools/renode/peripherals/NRF52840_Temp.cs

mach create "rak4631"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/nrf52840.repl
machine LoadPlatformDescription @tools/renode/ficr.repl
machine LoadPlatformDescription @tools/renode/uicr.repl
machine LoadPlatformDescription @tools/renode/temp.repl

: Erased flash under everything. This is not tidiness - the MBR tests words
: against 0xFFFFFFFF to decide whether things exist, and Renode's memory starts
: at zero, so on a bare machine every such test answers "present" and it
: dereferences a null pointer. That single difference is what made the published
: binaries look unrunnable.
sysbus LoadBinary @/tmp/erased_flash.bin 0x0
sysbus LoadBinary @/tmp/erased_uicr.bin 0x10001000

: Then the real regions, in flash order.
sysbus LoadBinary @/tmp/s140.bin 0x0
sysbus LoadBinary @/tmp/boot_00000000.bin 0x0
sysbus LoadBinary @/tmp/boot_000f4000.bin 0xF4000
sysbus LoadBinary @/tmp/boot_000fd800.bin 0xFD800
sysbus LoadBinary @/tmp/boot_10001000.bin 0x10001000
sysbus LoadBinary @/tmp/rak.bin 0x26000

: The MBR boots first, so SP and PC come from ITS vector table at 0. Setting
: only VectorTableOffset leaves SP uninitialised and the firmware faults within
: 45 instructions pushing an exception frame to a bogus stack.
cpu VectorTableOffset 0x0
cpu SP `sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x0`
cpu PC `sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x4`

include @/tmp/ficr_writes.txt
logLevel 3
